title: Proposition 1
---
order: 1
---
short_label: XII.1
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Similar polygons inscribed in circles are to one another as the squares on their diameters.
----
proof:

Let *ABC* and *FGH* be circles, let *ABCDE* and *FGHKL* be similar polygons inscribed in them, and let *BM* and *GN* be diameters of the circles.

I say that the square on *BM* is to the square on *GN* as the polygon *ABCDE* is to the polygon *FGHKL.*

Join *BE, AM, GL,* and *FN.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="440" height="250" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XII.1 diagram" src="propXII1.gif"/></noscript>
